  "status_text": "Several graphs we walked today turned out cheaper than our own circuits said, so the hunt now asks the crowd whether these will too. A generated family of 8 by 8 graphs, half their cells filled and no two rows or columns alike, is on the desk: for each we hold one circuit of our own (computed, not checked), and each unit asks for a smaller one, for example at most 27 AND/OR gates of fan-in two on one-a-side inputs [L-meta-19938, a conjecture]. A graph that will not get cheaper is where a floor gets tried.",
